#[$in title:["Project structure"]]
#[$in description:["How Moth projects are structured, how modules are discovered and how the HTML builder emits pages."]]
#[$in head:[language_theme_head]]

#[navbar]
#[sidebar]
init_docs_sidebar()!
#[section, $md:
    # Project structure

    A Moth project combines directory-scoped modules, an optional root-level
    project config and a builder that selects the final artefacts.

    Normal module roots start with `@`. Support and package-facade roots start
    with `+`. The rest of the filename stays cosmetic. `export:` currently
    defines the public API. `$page` will declare HTML artefacts; today the
    builder still selects entries from implemented root activity.
]

